WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.455
Read the condition
Consider the set of triples whose coordinates sum to zero. We will prove that
it is a subspace, then find an explicit basis.

2
00:00:13.455 --> 00:00:27.818
Prove the subspace property
The zero vector belongs to the set. A real linear combination of two solutions
still has coordinate sum zero, so closure under linear combinations holds.

3
00:00:27.818 --> 00:00:40.364
Parametrize
Choose y and z as free parameters. The equation forces x to equal minus y
minus z, giving a parametric representation.

4
00:00:40.364 --> 00:00:54.273
Find spanning vectors
Collect the terms for each parameter separately. Every element becomes s times
one vector plus t times another, so these vectors span the space.

5
00:00:54.273 --> 00:01:10.000
Check linear independence
To check independence, suppose the combination is the zero vector. The second
coordinate forces s to be zero, and the third forces t to be zero as well.

6
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:24.818
Conclude
The family is spanning and linearly independent, so it is a basis. It contains
two vectors, giving dimension two, even though the elements have three
coordinates.
